module

public import
StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MoreMorphisms.RegularIdealSheaf.RegularFromRelativeQuasiRegular
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MoreMorphisms.RelativeRegularImmersion.AffineQuasiRegular
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MoreMorphisms.RelativeRegularImmersion.FlatnessSpreadOut
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.Immersion

/-!
# Stacks tag 063W reduced to an affine chart

`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Statement063W` asks, near a point `x` of a closed subscheme `T` of a
scheme `X` flat and locally of finite presentation over `S`, for an open on which `T` is a
relative quasi-regular immersion over `S` and a regular immersion.  Three of the four things that
statement needs are available:

* the regular immersion is free, by Stacks tag 063U
  (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.statement063W_of_exists_isRelativeQuasiRegularImmersion`);
* the flatness of `T` over `S` near `x` spreads out from the point, by openness of the flat locus
  (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.exists_mem_flat_subschemeι_comap`);
* an affine open carrying a weakly regular generating family for the ideal of `T` makes the
  restriction of `T` a quasi-regular immersion
  (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isQuasiRegularImmersion_comap_of_isWeaklyRegular`).

So the whole of `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Statement063W` rests on one statement about affine
charts, `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ChartInput063W`:  inside any prescribed open neighbourhood of
`x` there is an affine open over which the ideal of `T` is generated by a weakly regular family.
That is the pointwise spreading out of Stacks tags 062Y (3) and 046Y, whose ring-theoretic
content is already in this library.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ChartInput063W`: the affine-chart statement that remains.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.statement063W_of_chartInput063W`:
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ChartInput063W` implies
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Statement063W`.

## Implementation notes

`ChartInput063W` carries the prescribed neighbourhood `V₀` because the chart has to be chosen
inside the open on which flatness of `T` over `S` is already known;  the ring-theoretic spreading
out shrinks the chart freely, so this costs nothing.

The fibre hypothesis of `ChartInput063W` is the one of `Statement063W` verbatim.  Its
ring-theoretic translation — a family of elements of the ideal that `T` cuts out in `𝒪_{X, x}`
whose classes in the local ring of the fibre form a regular sequence generating that ideal — is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.exists_mem_stalkIdeal_isRegular_quotient`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.22.8 (Tag 063W)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063W)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.22.4 (Tag 063U)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063U)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 062Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/062Y)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 046Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/046Y)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace AlgebraicGeometry RingTheory.Sequence
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

/-- **The affine-chart input of Stacks tag 063W.**  Under the hypotheses of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Statement063W`, every open neighbourhood of the point contains an
affine open over which the ideal of the closed subscheme is generated by a family of sections
which is weakly regular in the ring of sections. -/
abbrev ChartInput063W : Prop :=
  ∀ {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S), Flat f → LocallyOfFinitePresentation f →
    ∀ (T : X.IdealSheafData), LocallyOfFinitePresentation T.subschemeι →
      ∀ (x : X) (hx : x ∈ T.support),
        (∃ V : (f.fiber (f x)).Opens, f.asFiber x ∈ V ∧ IsQuasiRegularImmersion
          (((T.comap (f.fiberι (f x))).comap V.ι).subschemeι)) →
        ((T.subschemeι ≫ f).stalkMap (⟨x, hx⟩ : T.subscheme)).hom.Flat →
        ∀ V₀ : X.Opens, x ∈ V₀ →
          ∃ (V : X.Opens) (hV : IsAffineOpen V), x ∈ V ∧ V ≤ V₀ ∧
            ∃ (r : ℕ) (c : Fin r → Γ(X, V)), T.ideal ⟨V, hV⟩ = Ideal.span (Set.range c) ∧
              IsWeaklyRegular Γ(X, V) (List.ofFn c)

/-- **The affine-chart input gives the whole of Stacks tag 063W's "equality_flat" clause.**
Flatness over the base comes from openness of the flat locus, quasi-regularity of the immersion
from the weakly regular generating family on the affine chart, and the regular immersion from
Stacks tag 063U. -/
theorem statement063W_of_chartInput063W (h : ChartInput063W.{u}) : Statement063W.{u} := by
  refine statement063W_of_exists_isRelativeQuasiRegularImmersion ?_
  intro X S f hf hfp T hT x hx hfib hflat
  have _ := hfp
  have _ := hT
  obtain ⟨V₀, hxV₀, hflatV⟩ := exists_mem_flat_subschemeι_comap f T x hx hflat
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hxV, hVV₀, r, c, hgen, hwr⟩ := h f hf hfp T hT x hx hfib hflat V₀ hxV₀
  exact ⟨V, hxV, hflatV V hVV₀,
    isQuasiRegularImmersion_comap_of_isWeaklyRegular T hV c hgen hwr⟩

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry

end
